# ── Frontend environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# VITE_API_URL — base URL of the backend REST API, including the `/api` suffix.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite resolves `import.meta.env.*` at BUILD time, not at runtime.
# The value is inlined into the generated bundle by `npm run build`, so:
#
#   * Changing it afterwards requires a NEW BUILD — editing `.env` (or the
#     server's environment) on an already-built `dist/` has no effect.
#   * Its absence FAILS a production bundle, loudly and on purpose.
#     `services/api.config.ts` throws while the module loads when
#     `import.meta.env.PROD` is true and the variable is unset, so the app
#     refuses to start with a message naming VITE_API_URL. It used to fall back
#     silently to `http://localhost:3000/api` instead, which shipped a build
#     that looked fine and wasn't: every user's browser called its own machine
#     and every screen reported "Could not reach the server".
#   * An EMPTY value (`VITE_API_URL=`) is treated as absent and fails the same
#     way. It is not a way to get same-origin requests any more — write
#     `VITE_API_URL=/api` explicitly for that (see the reverse-proxy example
#     below). Previously the empty string survived `??` and every request went
#     out relative to the origin serving the app, which was indistinguishable
#     from a misconfiguration.
#   * DEVELOPMENT is unchanged. With `import.meta.env.PROD` false — `npm run
#     dev`, `vitest` — an absent variable still falls back to
#     `http://localhost:3000/api` and nothing throws.
#
# Local development against a backend on the same machine:
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
#
# Team testing against a shared dev machine (note `vite.config.ts` sets
# `server.host = true`, so the dev server is reachable on the LAN):
# VITE_API_URL=http://10.222.68.106:3000/api
#
# Production build (example — use the real deployed API host):
# VITE_API_URL=https://ssd.nexteer.com/api
#
# Production build where the API is reverse-proxied under the same origin as
# the app (this is what the old empty value meant, now spelled out):
# VITE_API_URL=/api
